    "body": "RV32E and RV64E are ratified, but we shouldn't instantly mark ILP32E and LP64E as being finalised. For instance, it looks like we don't properly document the alignment on ILP32E for 2xlen types - where I believe _only on the stack_ these types are 4-byte aligned in GCC? (The note about the stack being 4-byte aligned and the D extension not being compatible is relevant - but you could have a 4 byte stack and require it to be realigned for stack objects that need greater alignment).",
